### 🧩 Line-by-Line Breakdown

| Line | What It Does | Memory Picture |
|------|----------------|----------------|
| `struct Node { ... };` | Defines blueprint for each tree node | Each node = data + left ptr + right ptr |
| `createNode()` | Allocates memory for new node and sets its data | Like building a new box with empty left/right branches |
| `root = createNode(1);` | Makes first node (root) | Root = top of tree |
| `root->left = createNode(2);` | Creates left child of root | 1 → 2 link |
| `root->right = createNode(3);` | Creates right child of root | 1 → 3 link |
| `preorder()` | Prints values in Root→Left→Right order | 1, 2, 4, 5, 3 |

🧠 **Remember**:  
> “Preorder means parent first.”  
